<h2 id="ir-when" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. When this applies</h2>

| Trigger | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| **<code>implref</code>** | User attaches or names a refactor plan **Markdown** path (typically under <code>cursor_gen/</code> or docs). Execute the procedure below against **that file** unless they specify otherwise. |
| **<code>resumimpl</code>** | User wants to **continue** the same refactor plan after a block or interruption: re-read the plan, respect already marked <code>[X]</code> items, continue from the first incomplete phase. |

If the message does not name a plan file, **infer** the most recently discussed plan in the thread; if still ambiguous, ask **one** precise question: which path is the plan?

---

<h2 id="ir-shape" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. Refactor plan document shape (<code>[ ]</code> / <code>[X]</code>)</h2>

The plan **Markdown** MUST be workable as a checklist:

- **Major sections:** Numbered phases (example: **1. Phase A**, **2. Phase B**, …) with matching **outline** at the top of the doc (mirrors MRKD document-outline pattern).
- **Items:** Each implementable bullet or phase-level deliverable prefixed with **`[ ]`** (not done) or **`[X]`** (done).
- **Phase headings:** Optionally prefix the **phase heading line** itself with **`[X]`** when **all** bullets in that phase are complete — e.g. <code>**[X] 3.** Phase C — …</code> — so scanners see progress “at the section title”; keep bullet-level <code>[X]</code> in sync.

If the referenced file mixes prose without phases, **reorganize** it (step 0) **before** implementation.

