<h2 id="ir-s3-move" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">9. Procedure: step 3.5 — relocate plan under <code>cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/</code> vs <code>cursor_gen/refactor_plans/wip/</code></h2>

Run this when an **`implref` / `resumimpl` engagement** ends: all requested work for this pass is done, you hit a true blocker, or the user stops the run—**after** saving the plan’s final **`[ ]` / `[X]`** state.

1. Ensure directories exist: **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/`** and **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/wip/`** (create them if missing).

2. **Checkbox taxonomy (before classifying the folder)** — Plans must not confuse **[§7 procedural step&nbsp;3](#ir-s3)** implementations or readers by pairing **`[ ]`** with prose that **is not** part of **`implref`'s in-repo commitments**.

   | Kind | SHOULD use **`[ ]` / `[X]`?** |
   |------|------------------------------|
   | Concrete deliverables inside **numbered phases** the **`implref`** pass is executing | **Yes** |
   | **Non-goals** (“we do **not** do X”) | **No** — use prose or empty tables; **`[ ]` looks like undone work** |
   | **Explicitly optional adjuncts** (debug logging spikes, multiset, operator-only staging narratives) named *optional / product-gated* | Prefer **Deferred** section **without** phased **`[ ]`**; otherwise **`wip/`** if left as orphaned **`[ ]`** in phased lists |
   | **Out-of-repo checklists** (manual staging QA) | **No** phased boxes tied to **`implref`** |

   Before **`git mv`** to **`completed/`**: satisfy **implementable** **`[ ]`**, **`[X]`** waive skipped items **with rationale**, migrate leftovers **into Deferred** without duplicate boxes — or classify plan **`wip/`** if phased **`[ ]`** remain honest TODOs.

3. **Classify completion**

   - **3.1 `completed/` (core shipped).** Using **item&nbsp;2 taxonomy**, every **implementable** phased row under **`implref`'s scope is **`[X]`** — *or* cleanly waived per item&nbsp;2 — and **numbered phases** contain **no leftover misleading `[ ]`** rows. Rename phase headings **`[X]`** when justified. Closing **step&nbsp;4** names any **waived optional** scope.

     **Mismatch guard:** if implementable phased **`[ ]`** still denote **skipped required work**, use **`wip/`** (or fix Markdown); do **not** place the doc in **`completed/`**—“use judgment” is **not** a bypass for orphaned TODO boxes.

     **Purely informational** sections plus Markdown **tables whose rows omit `[ ]` / `[X]` entirely** do **not** block **`completed/`**.

   - **3.2 `wip/`**. Honest phased TODOs **`[ ]`**, **`§3.1e`** cuts, **`§3.1d`** blocker, or **`resumimpl`** expected → **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/wip/`**.

4. **Path rules** (folder meanings: **onlyref** [Plan folder lifecycle](.cursor/rules/onlyref-refactor-plan-author-only.mdc#onlyref-folders) — do not duplicate that table here)
   - Ensure **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/new/`**, **`wip/`**, and **`completed/`** exist.
   - Plan in **`new/`** and **first** implementable phased **`[X]`** in this pass → **`git mv`** to **`wip/`** (same basename).
   - Plan in **`wip/`** or **`new/`** when **item&nbsp;3.1** satisfied → **`git mv`** to **`completed/`**.
   - Plan already in **`wip/`** or **`completed/`** → **move between** those two when status **changes**; do not move back to **`new/`**.
   - Plans at **`cursor_gen/<file>.md`** (root only) → **`wip/`** or **`completed/`** per **item&nbsp;3** above.
   - Plans **outside** **`cursor_gen/`**: default **`git mv` / copy** under **`wip/`** or **`completed/`** unless the user keeps a canonical path elsewhere—state **both** in step&nbsp;4.

5. **Deferred dedupe.** Deferred / follow-ups **must not duplicate** phased **`[ ]`** after closeout; **one canonical** home — prefer Deferred tables/prose rows that **omit** `[ ]` / `[X]` for backlog items.

